WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:08.257
Hello, hello, hello, and welcome

00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:10.187
to English Learning for Curious

00:00:10.187 --> 00:00:13.167
Minds, by Leonardo English, the show

00:00:13.177 --> 00:00:14.977
where you can listen to fascinating

00:00:14.977 --> 00:00:17.477
stories and learn weird and wonderful

00:00:17.487 --> 00:00:19.577
things about the world at the same

00:00:19.577 --> 00:00:21.377
time as improving your English.

00:00:21.857 --> 00:00:24.767
I'm Alastair Budge, and today we

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.377
are going to be talking about a

00:00:26.407 --> 00:00:29.505
Swedish man called Raoul Wallenberg.

00:00:30.257 --> 00:00:33.765
This is a story of war, neutrality,

00:00:33.765 --> 00:00:36.801
savagery, bravery, and a mission

00:00:37.011 --> 00:00:39.041
that should have been impossible.

00:00:39.741 --> 00:00:41.621
OK then, let's not waste a

00:00:41.621 --> 00:00:44.301
minute and get right into it.

00:00:45.791 --> 00:00:47.991
Many languages have some

00:00:48.051 --> 00:00:50.321
variant of the saying "you're

00:00:50.351 --> 00:00:52.631
either with us or against us".

00:00:53.461 --> 00:00:56.411
It's a rebuke of neutrality, a way

00:00:56.411 --> 00:00:58.681
of saying you can't just shrug your

00:00:58.681 --> 00:01:01.371
shoulders and say "I'm staying out of it".

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:05.681
And this was especially true in the

00:01:05.681 --> 00:01:09.491
Europe of the late 1930s, a Europe where

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:12.251
on one side there was Nazi Germany,

00:01:12.531 --> 00:01:15.191
united with Fascist Italy, and on the

00:01:15.221 --> 00:01:18.131
other the Allied coalition, initially

00:01:18.351 --> 00:01:21.251
consisting of the UK, France, and Poland.

00:01:22.411 --> 00:01:25.731
As the war continued, most European

00:01:25.731 --> 00:01:27.911
nations declared themselves

00:01:28.111 --> 00:01:30.861
allied to one side or the other.

00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:34.561
Some managed to remain neutral.

00:01:35.391 --> 00:01:37.501
Ireland, Portugal and Spain

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.901
declared themselves neutral, or

00:01:40.071 --> 00:01:42.981
non-belligerent, and for the most

00:01:42.981 --> 00:01:45.111
part stayed out of the conflict.

00:01:45.951 --> 00:01:48.571
Switzerland, too, remained neutral.

00:01:49.121 --> 00:01:52.091
But Swiss neutrality rested on

00:01:52.091 --> 00:01:53.861
a slightly different foundation.

00:01:54.491 --> 00:01:57.561
It was mountainous, heavily armed, and

00:01:57.571 --> 00:02:00.521
had long cultivated an identity built

00:02:00.571 --> 00:02:03.671
around staying outside European wars.

00:02:04.201 --> 00:02:06.711
So even though it was much closer

00:02:06.711 --> 00:02:09.341
to the action, it managed to escape

00:02:09.531 --> 00:02:11.661
getting dragged into the conflict.

00:02:13.011 --> 00:02:15.091
And then there was Sweden.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:19.040
Like Switzerland, Sweden had a

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.310
long tradition of neutrality.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:25.100
But unlike Ireland, Portugal,

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.900
or Spain, Sweden was much

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.320
closer to the theatre of war.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.210
And by the middle of

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.940
1940, it was surrounded.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.110
In the space of two months, both

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.880
of its western neighbours had

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.370
been swallowed up by Nazi Germany.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.220
Norway and Denmark were

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.250
both under German control.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.840
To the east was Finland, which

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.920
had fought the Soviet Union in the

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.980
Winter War and would soon align

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.000
itself with Germany against Moscow.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:05.490
The official Swedish policy was that of

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.240
neutrality, but this would prove much

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.540
harder in practice than it was in theory.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.350
Sweden continued to sell iron ore to

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.970
Nazi Germany throughout the war — the

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.340
raw material that fed the production

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.960
of bullets, tanks, ships and bombs.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.160
Sweden let Nazi Germany move troops

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.870
across its borders, first between

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.960
Germany and Norway, and then more

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:37.690
controversially, eastwards towards

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.370
Russia as part of Operation Barbarossa,

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.970
the invasion of the Soviet Union.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.060
And unlike most European countries,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.770
Sweden emerged from the war physically

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.110
unscathed and in a relatively strong

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.380
economic position, something that

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.710
would help lay the foundations for

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.960
the prosperity it enjoys today.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.120
So it is perfectly reasonable to argue

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.380
that Sweden, in the 1940s, was not

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:11.910
merely standing aside, but actively

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.530
helping sustain the Nazi war machine.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:17.760
In other words, its neutrality

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.830
came at a moral cost.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.110
There is one man, however, at whom

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:27.030
such criticism cannot be raised.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.980
His name was Raoul Wallenberg.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.140
He came from the pre-eminent

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:36.570
Swedish family, the Wallenbergs,

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:38.890
or the Wallenbergs, to give

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.710
them their Anglicised name.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.940
And it's hard to overstate quite how

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.660
much power and influence the Wallenbergs

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.660
had back then and still have today.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.570
They controlled the main bank

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.370
in Sweden, and held major stakes

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.860
in most major Swedish companies.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.220
But today we will not be talking

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.660
about Raoul's business dealings,

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.450
but something much more important,

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.150
more lasting, and more human.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.404
He was born in 1912.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:17.100
He was a Wallenberg, so he grew up

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.640
in the family's world of business and

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:22.500
international commerce, but he wasn't

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.980
directly in the line of succession.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:28.740
As such, his upbringing was slightly

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.030
different to that of his cousins at

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.460
the core of the family empire, who

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.680
were being groomed for succession.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.100
He was sent to the United

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.190
States to study architecture.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.030
He was already fluent in French and

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.040
German, but his time in the US meant

00:05:46.161 --> 00:05:48.280
he could add English to this list.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.530
He was, by all accounts, charming

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.850
and perceptive, comfortable in

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:57.960
many worlds, but a little bit lost,

00:05:58.281 --> 00:06:00.520
directionless, after graduating from

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.720
university and returning to Sweden.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.560
He found that his American architecture

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:09.070
degree wasn't actually valid in

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.950
Sweden, and so he drifted between

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.270
jobs arranged by family members.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.500
One of these was in Haifa, which was

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.450
then part of British Palestine, and

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.290
it was here that he met a large number

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.460
of German Jews who had fled the Nazis.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:32.810
This was in 1936, and although it would

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:35.790
be several years before the persecution

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:39.290
of Jews reached its peak, anti-Semitism

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:41.900
was rampant, and there were an

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.840
increasing number of anti-Jewish laws.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:49.370
The Wallenberg family is not Jewish,

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:52.330
but Raoul Wallenberg had a Jewish

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:55.200
great-great-grandfather, technically

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.810
making him one-sixteenth Jewish.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.110
And he was, apparently,

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.340
very proud of this heritage.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.440
At a time when many Jews were,

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.500
perfectly understandably, trying

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.690
to disguise their background,

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:13.610
Raoul Wallenberg leaned into it.

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.680
And he saw firsthand the

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.120
persecution that Jews across

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.120
Europe were increasingly facing.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.070
First, through business.

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.300
He worked at a trading company in

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.910
Stockholm, and saw that his boss — who was

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:35.400
a Hungarian Jew — he was finding it harder

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.750
and harder to move around in Europe.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:42.020
Hungary had passed anti-Jewish laws in

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:46.450
1938, and when Hungary officially allied

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:50.370
with Nazi Germany in 1940, well, its

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.250
policy towards its Jewish community looked

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.110
increasingly like its newfound ally's.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:00.080
Wallenberg travelled a lot for his

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.870
work — to Hungary, to France, and

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:06.200
to Germany — and he became the 1940s

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.650
equivalent of the sort of person who

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:10.860
knows exactly how to get through security

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.820
control in the quickest queue and without

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:16.030
the metal detector ever going off.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:20.390
In his case, this meant paperwork

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.070
— he knew which papers you needed,

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.380
which stamps, which signatures.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.570
It might sound like a meaningless

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.770
detail, but it would prove

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.200
of vital importance later on.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.250
Now, the important thing to emphasise here

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.760
is that Wallenberg was a businessman, a

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.840
businessman of a neutral country, Sweden.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:47.580
But he knew about what was happening

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:51.360
to European Jews, he had this sliver of

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:55.190
Jewish ancestry himself, and he decided

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.300
he was going to do something about it.

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:02.540
In June 1944, he was introduced to a man

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:05.299
named Iver Olsen, who was the Stockholm

00:09:05.299 --> 00:09:08.130
representative of the United States War

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:11.352
Refugee Board, or the WRB for short.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.420
This was an agency created by President

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:19.160
Roosevelt with a specific mandate: to

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:22.330
use American resources and influence to

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:25.150
rescue civilians from Nazi persecution.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:28.340
And the civilians who were being most

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:30.730
heavily persecuted were the Jews.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:35.340
Olsen needed someone to go to Budapest.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:38.730
Someone who could work under diplomatic

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:41.320
cover, who understood the terrain,

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:43.770
who had the right combination of nerve

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:46.500
and practicality for something very

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:49.590
difficult in very dangerous circumstances.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:52.330
He chose Wallenberg.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:55.670
Now, Wallenberg negotiated

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.690
his own terms before agreeing.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.290
He wanted real authority to operate

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.920
independently, without being constrained

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:05.990
by what the Swedish diplomatic mission

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.710
in Budapest was comfortable with.

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:10.440
He wanted money to bribe officials.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.740
He wanted freedom to do whatever it took.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.240
Carte blanche.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.040
The Swedish government agreed.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:21.600
He was appointed First Secretary of

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:24.110
the Swedish legation in Budapest,

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.780
which gave him diplomatic cover and

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:29.250
the authority of a Swedish passport.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.160
In early 1944, he packed a

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.710
rucksack, a sleeping bag, and a

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:38.260
revolver, and set off for Hungary.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:41.400
Budapest, to be precise, one of the

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.690
last great concentrations of Jews

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.590
still alive in Nazi-dominated Europe.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:50.110
Wallenberg was thirty-one years

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:52.830
old, and he had never been asked

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.910
to do anything like this before.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:58.960
Now, to understand what Wallenberg was

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:01.490
walking into, we need to understand

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:03.740
what had already happened in Hungary

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:05.910
in the weeks before he arrived.

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:10.560
Hungary had gone over to the Axis powers

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:14.390
in 1940, but when the war turned for

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:17.400
Nazi Germany, Hungary had started to

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.980
secretly negotiate with the Allies.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:24.550
When Hitler found out about this, in early

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:28.250
1944, he ordered the invasion of Hungary.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:32.710
It was largely peaceful, and barely a

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.860
shot was fired, but the relevance for

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:39.879
our story is that by March of 1944,

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:43.210
Hungary was under German occupation.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:47.580
And Hungary had a relatively large

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:51.740
Jewish population, some 700,000, half

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.540
of which lived in Budapest, the capital.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:58.690
And Hungary's Jewish community had been

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:01.890
persecuted, stripped of rights, and forced

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:05.200
into labour brigades, but, importantly,

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:08.640
most had survived; the deportations

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:11.320
to the death camps had not yet begun.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:15.120
However, among the first Nazi

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.780
officials to arrive in occupied

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:19.060
Hungary was Adolf Eichmann.

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:22.520
He was one of the key architects

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.480
of the holocaust, the Nazi

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:26.970
official responsible for overseeing

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.760
deportations across occupied Europe.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:33.680
He arrived in Budapest in March

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.480
1944 and set up his office

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.550
in a large downtown hotel.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:41.830
He moved with terrifying

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:43.800
and extraordinary speed.

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.760
Between the 15th of May and the

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:51.700
9th of July 1944, approximately

00:12:52.083 --> 00:12:57.040
437,000 Hungarian Jews were

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.890
packed onto trains and sent north.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:02.980
Almost all of them went to

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:05.040
Auschwitz, where most were

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:06.890
killed as soon as they arrived.

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:10.550
Wallenberg arrived in Budapest

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.320
on the 9th of July 1944.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.940
Two days earlier, Hungary’s regent,

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:19.380
Miklós Horthy, had suspended

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:21.510
the deportations under immense

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:24.120
international pressure, including a

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:26.510
personal letter from the Swedish king.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:31.120
So when Wallenberg reached the Swedish

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:34.380
legation, the trains had just stopped.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.560
But there were still around

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:41.320
200,000 Jews remaining in Budapest.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.660
And as to whether the deportations

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:47.090
would resume, nobody knew.

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:50.260
Eichmann was still in the city.

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.940
The Arrow Cross, Hungary's

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.340
fascist party, was pushing hard

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.410
for deportations to continue.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.470
The situation was unstable,

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:03.780
the threat immediate, and the

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.130
margin for error was very small.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:10.980
And Wallenberg arrived with a tool that

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:13.510
looked, at first glance, completely

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.260
inadequate compared to the scale of the

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:19.380
task ahead of him: a protective passport.

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:23.380
The Schutzpass, as it came to be known,

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:26.030
was a formally printed document in

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.860
the blue and yellow colours of the

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.700
Swedish flag, stamped with Sweden’s

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.960
triple-crown seal, declaring the

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.400
bearer to be under Swedish protection

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.209
and awaiting repatriation to Sweden.

00:14:39.839 --> 00:14:42.523
In theory, this was shaky.

00:14:43.083 --> 00:14:45.643
These were not fully legal documents.

00:14:45.803 --> 00:14:48.853
They had no firm basis in international

00:14:48.863 --> 00:14:52.113
law, and Sweden had no clear

00:14:52.363 --> 00:14:54.773
legal right to extend this kind

00:14:54.773 --> 00:14:57.053
of protection to Hungarian Jews.

00:14:58.363 --> 00:15:00.583
In practice, however, the

00:15:00.583 --> 00:15:02.283
document often worked.

00:15:03.023 --> 00:15:05.803
It looked official, it came from a

00:15:05.803 --> 00:15:08.913
neutral state, and in the confusion

00:15:08.913 --> 00:15:13.063
and uncertainty of late 1944, that

00:15:13.073 --> 00:15:15.573
was often enough to make Hungarian

00:15:15.573 --> 00:15:17.993
or German officials hesitate.

00:15:19.153 --> 00:15:21.083
Now, these papers were not

00:15:21.083 --> 00:15:23.103
simply handed out at random.

00:15:23.663 --> 00:15:26.543
Jews in Budapest tried to obtain them

00:15:26.833 --> 00:15:28.743
through the Swedish mission and the

00:15:28.743 --> 00:15:31.063
wider rescue network forming around it,

00:15:31.393 --> 00:15:34.213
and those who secured one could then

00:15:34.253 --> 00:15:36.493
claim to be under Swedish protection.

00:15:37.903 --> 00:15:39.663
The Swedish foreign ministry

00:15:39.913 --> 00:15:42.063
had originally approved

00:15:42.303 --> 00:15:44.593
1,500 protective passes.

00:15:45.014 --> 00:15:47.724
Wallenberg pushed, improvised, and

00:15:47.944 --> 00:15:50.094
bribed where necessary, and the

00:15:50.094 --> 00:15:52.814
number rose dramatically, with some

00:15:52.814 --> 00:15:55.931
estimates putting it at around 15,000.

00:15:57.376 --> 00:15:59.284
But the Schutzpass was

00:15:59.294 --> 00:16:00.744
only part of the system.

00:16:01.734 --> 00:16:04.264
Wallenberg also took over more than

00:16:04.294 --> 00:16:07.464
thirty buildings across Budapest, flew

00:16:07.514 --> 00:16:10.564
Swedish flags above them, and declared

00:16:10.564 --> 00:16:13.024
them to be under Swedish protection.

00:16:14.334 --> 00:16:18.214
These became refuge houses: overcrowded,

00:16:18.494 --> 00:16:21.174
makeshift safe houses for Jews who had

00:16:21.174 --> 00:16:23.774
received Swedish papers, or who were

00:16:23.774 --> 00:16:26.104
trying to come under Swedish protection.

00:16:27.294 --> 00:16:29.374
The legal basis for these

00:16:29.374 --> 00:16:31.434
houses was flimsy, just as it

00:16:31.434 --> 00:16:33.134
was for the Schutzpass itself.

00:16:33.424 --> 00:16:36.284
But once again, the appearance

00:16:36.404 --> 00:16:38.614
of Swedish authority often bought

00:16:38.674 --> 00:16:41.974
time, and sometimes that was the

00:16:41.974 --> 00:16:43.834
difference between life and death.

00:16:45.194 --> 00:16:47.964
And for a few brief months,

00:16:48.224 --> 00:16:50.084
that fragile system held.

00:16:50.794 --> 00:16:54.634
But in October 1944, whatever

00:16:54.854 --> 00:16:57.724
fragile stability remained collapsed.

00:16:58.664 --> 00:17:01.134
The regent of Hungary, Miklós Horthy,

00:17:01.444 --> 00:17:04.424
was removed from power and the Arrow

00:17:04.464 --> 00:17:06.964
Cross took control of Budapest.

00:17:08.004 --> 00:17:09.504
The situation became

00:17:09.504 --> 00:17:11.224
considerably more dangerous.

00:17:11.994 --> 00:17:15.004
The Arrow Cross was a Hungarian fascist

00:17:15.034 --> 00:17:17.894
party with a particular streak of

00:17:17.904 --> 00:17:21.064
vicious antisemitism, and they were

00:17:21.064 --> 00:17:24.454
not interested in diplomatic niceties.

00:17:25.734 --> 00:17:28.324
Within days of taking power, they

00:17:28.324 --> 00:17:30.834
had begun executing Jews on the

00:17:30.844 --> 00:17:33.164
banks of the Danube, shooting them

00:17:33.454 --> 00:17:34.924
and throwing them into the river.

00:17:35.914 --> 00:17:37.604
This was the moment when

00:17:37.604 --> 00:17:39.924
Wallenberg’s work became even more

00:17:39.924 --> 00:17:42.584
dangerous, and even more direct.

00:17:43.534 --> 00:17:46.004
He was no longer simply issuing

00:17:46.004 --> 00:17:48.664
papers from behind a desk or moving

00:17:48.664 --> 00:17:50.354
people into protected houses.

00:17:50.634 --> 00:17:52.474
He was now confronting the

00:17:52.474 --> 00:17:54.494
aggressors in real time.

00:17:55.734 --> 00:17:57.884
He showed up wherever Jews were

00:17:57.884 --> 00:18:00.014
being rounded up and driven away.

00:18:00.404 --> 00:18:03.004
He handed out Schutzpasses, argued

00:18:03.004 --> 00:18:04.994
with guards, and demanded the

00:18:04.994 --> 00:18:07.424
release of anyone he could plausibly

00:18:07.454 --> 00:18:09.704
claim was under Swedish protection.

00:18:10.854 --> 00:18:13.674
When deportation convoys were assembled

00:18:13.684 --> 00:18:15.294
at the city’s railway stations,

00:18:15.714 --> 00:18:17.974
Wallenberg would appear in person.

00:18:18.564 --> 00:18:21.894
He produced lists, cited his authority,

00:18:22.194 --> 00:18:25.374
and spoke with the calm certainty of

00:18:25.374 --> 00:18:27.744
someone who expected to be obeyed.

00:18:28.784 --> 00:18:30.584
Much of it was bluff.

00:18:30.744 --> 00:18:32.784
But the bluff worked.

00:18:34.134 --> 00:18:36.034
He could not save everyone.

00:18:36.404 --> 00:18:39.884
But every person he did save was one

00:18:39.894 --> 00:18:42.637
less passenger on the train to Auschwitz.

00:18:44.164 --> 00:18:46.714
And under the Arrow Cross, the

00:18:46.714 --> 00:18:49.874
persecution had become even more brutal.

00:18:50.934 --> 00:18:53.384
Jews were being forced on death

00:18:53.424 --> 00:18:56.424
marches, forced to walk westward

00:18:56.644 --> 00:18:58.644
toward the Austrian border, in

00:18:58.654 --> 00:19:01.834
winter, with no food and no shelter.

00:19:03.074 --> 00:19:05.294
Wallenberg followed the marches.

00:19:05.654 --> 00:19:08.174
He walked along the columns, handing out

00:19:08.174 --> 00:19:10.814
Schutzpasses to people who had nothing.

00:19:11.244 --> 00:19:13.924
He argued for their release at gunpoint.

00:19:14.664 --> 00:19:17.654
More than once, he even ran alongside

00:19:17.664 --> 00:19:19.984
moving trains, passing documents

00:19:20.054 --> 00:19:21.954
through the windows to those

00:19:21.964 --> 00:19:24.684
already inside and pulling them out

00:19:24.834 --> 00:19:26.524
before the train could get away.

00:19:27.794 --> 00:19:29.264
He had been in Budapest

00:19:29.434 --> 00:19:30.844
for only six months.

00:19:31.854 --> 00:19:35.134
In that time, his operation had grown

00:19:35.144 --> 00:19:37.524
from one man with a rucksack into

00:19:37.524 --> 00:19:40.204
a network with hundreds of staff, a

00:19:40.214 --> 00:19:43.334
fleet of vehicles, thirty-two protected

00:19:43.334 --> 00:19:45.854
buildings, and a logistics operation

00:19:46.144 --> 00:19:48.224
that was feeding, sheltering, and

00:19:48.244 --> 00:19:51.164
documenting tens of thousands of people.

00:19:52.654 --> 00:19:56.604
And by mid-January 1945, it

00:19:56.604 --> 00:19:58.524
looked as if this extraordinary

00:19:58.524 --> 00:20:00.794
mission might be nearing its end.

00:20:02.034 --> 00:20:04.134
Soviet forces were fighting their

00:20:04.134 --> 00:20:06.564
way through the streets of Budapest.

00:20:07.124 --> 00:20:09.634
The Nazis were on the back foot.

00:20:10.674 --> 00:20:13.094
Wallenberg seems to have believed

00:20:13.284 --> 00:20:16.074
the Soviets would be natural allies.

00:20:16.734 --> 00:20:18.394
They were, after all,

00:20:18.604 --> 00:20:20.054
fighting Nazi Germany.

00:20:21.024 --> 00:20:22.854
By that logic, they

00:20:22.854 --> 00:20:23.974
should have been allies.

00:20:24.954 --> 00:20:28.064
So, he had a plan: to travel to meet

00:20:28.244 --> 00:20:31.214
Marshal Rodion Malinovsky, the Soviet

00:20:31.214 --> 00:20:34.144
commander, and negotiate the protection

00:20:34.364 --> 00:20:36.874
of Budapest's surviving Jewish community.

00:20:38.574 --> 00:20:40.044
He told colleagues he

00:20:40.044 --> 00:20:41.574
would be back in a week.

00:20:42.854 --> 00:20:46.204
On the 17th of January 1945, he

00:20:46.214 --> 00:20:48.454
set out for Soviet headquarters

00:20:48.594 --> 00:20:51.159
with his driver, Vilmos Langfelder.

00:20:52.194 --> 00:20:54.614
He was arrested almost immediately

00:20:54.834 --> 00:20:57.644
by agents from SMERSH, the Soviet

00:20:57.644 --> 00:20:59.544
military counterintelligence service.

00:21:00.704 --> 00:21:02.354
The stated reason was

00:21:02.384 --> 00:21:04.104
suspicion of espionage.

00:21:05.474 --> 00:21:08.484
Within days, he and his driver had

00:21:08.484 --> 00:21:11.794
been taken to Moscow and disappeared

00:21:12.024 --> 00:21:13.554
into the Soviet prison system.

00:21:15.374 --> 00:21:17.954
And I'm sorry to say that if you are

00:21:17.954 --> 00:21:20.224
hoping for a happy ending to this story,

00:21:20.624 --> 00:21:23.324
for Wallenberg at least, there is none.

00:21:24.364 --> 00:21:27.154
Nobody who knew him saw him again.

00:21:28.734 --> 00:21:31.634
And for twelve years, the Soviet

00:21:31.634 --> 00:21:33.694
government denied any knowledge

00:21:33.834 --> 00:21:35.304
of Wallenberg's whereabouts.

00:21:35.734 --> 00:21:38.064
He had simply vanished, as

00:21:38.064 --> 00:21:39.434
far as Moscow was concerned.

00:21:40.914 --> 00:21:42.884
During those years, his mother

00:21:43.064 --> 00:21:45.404
and stepfather wrote letters,

00:21:45.764 --> 00:21:48.384
lobbied officials, and refused

00:21:48.394 --> 00:21:49.964
to accept that he was gone.

00:21:50.904 --> 00:21:53.304
There were reported sightings from

00:21:53.314 --> 00:21:55.174
survivors of the Soviet camp system:

00:21:55.819 --> 00:21:59.204
Wallenberg in Lubyanka, Wallenberg in a

00:21:59.214 --> 00:22:02.274
camp in Siberia, even Wallenberg alive

00:22:02.484 --> 00:22:04.884
and asking to send word to Sweden.

00:22:06.084 --> 00:22:08.014
The Swedish government collected

00:22:08.024 --> 00:22:11.504
these reports but, by and large, sat

00:22:11.504 --> 00:22:13.844
on them, fearful of upsetting the

00:22:13.844 --> 00:22:15.724
relationship with the Soviet Union.

00:22:17.234 --> 00:22:20.294
Then, in 1957, the Soviets

00:22:20.344 --> 00:22:21.544
produced a document.

00:22:22.244 --> 00:22:24.534
It was signed by a Lubyanka prison

00:22:24.544 --> 00:22:27.854
doctor named Smoltsov, and it claimed

00:22:28.044 --> 00:22:30.584
that Wallenberg had died of a heart

00:22:30.614 --> 00:22:34.161
attack on the 17th of July 1947.

00:22:35.754 --> 00:22:37.244
The document was

00:22:37.594 --> 00:22:39.232
suspicious from the start.

00:22:40.244 --> 00:22:42.444
Smoltsov's own report used

00:22:42.444 --> 00:22:45.164
the phrase "seems to be" to

00:22:45.164 --> 00:22:46.554
describe the cause of death.

00:22:47.544 --> 00:22:49.434
The security chief had ordered

00:22:49.434 --> 00:22:51.314
that no autopsy be performed

00:22:51.494 --> 00:22:53.814
and that the body be cremated.

00:22:55.104 --> 00:22:57.954
And a Lubyanka prison log showed

00:22:58.174 --> 00:23:00.974
that a mysterious "Prisoner No. 7"

00:23:01.344 --> 00:23:03.564
had been questioned on the 23rd of

00:23:03.564 --> 00:23:07.884
July 1947, six days after the date

00:23:08.054 --> 00:23:09.894
of Wallenberg's supposed death.

00:23:11.134 --> 00:23:13.794
Over the following decades, various

00:23:13.804 --> 00:23:16.964
Soviet-era documents emerged suggesting

00:23:16.964 --> 00:23:19.074
that Wallenberg had been interrogated

00:23:19.104 --> 00:23:22.444
well into 1947, and possibly beyond.

00:23:23.564 --> 00:23:25.494
The KGB files on the case

00:23:25.814 --> 00:23:27.644
have never been fully opened.

00:23:29.004 --> 00:23:32.724
In 2016, the diaries of a man

00:23:32.764 --> 00:23:35.134
named Ivan Serov, a former

00:23:35.134 --> 00:23:37.234
KGB director, were published.

00:23:38.294 --> 00:23:40.304
Serov's entry on the Wallenberg

00:23:40.304 --> 00:23:42.424
case was unambiguous.

00:23:42.914 --> 00:23:45.304
"I have no doubts," he wrote, "that

00:23:45.304 --> 00:23:49.166
Wallenberg was liquidated in 1947."

00:23:50.144 --> 00:23:54.474
And it wouldn't be until 2016, when

00:23:54.474 --> 00:23:57.224
Raoul Wallenberg would have been 104

00:23:57.224 --> 00:24:00.054
years old, that he was officially

00:24:00.234 --> 00:24:03.094
declared dead by the Swedish Tax Agency.

00:24:04.584 --> 00:24:07.324
In terms of his impact, well, the

00:24:07.344 --> 00:24:09.394
estimates of how many lives he saved

00:24:09.434 --> 00:24:12.504
directly through the Schutzpass range

00:24:12.514 --> 00:24:15.234
from seven thousand to ten thousand.

00:24:16.064 --> 00:24:18.814
But his broader impact was almost

00:24:18.814 --> 00:24:20.454
certainly greater than that.

00:24:21.224 --> 00:24:24.634
When Soviet forces liberated Budapest in

00:24:24.634 --> 00:24:27.924
February 1945, around a hundred thousand

00:24:27.924 --> 00:24:30.034
Jews were still alive in the city.

00:24:31.154 --> 00:24:33.684
Had Eichmann succeeded in finishing

00:24:33.684 --> 00:24:35.984
the job he had begun in the spring and

00:24:35.984 --> 00:24:39.574
summer of 1944, that number would have

00:24:39.574 --> 00:24:42.664
been vastly lower, perhaps close to zero.

00:24:43.954 --> 00:24:46.224
The consensus among historians is

00:24:46.224 --> 00:24:48.504
that Wallenberg, together with the

00:24:48.524 --> 00:24:50.234
other neutral diplomats working

00:24:50.254 --> 00:24:52.104
alongside him, was one of the

00:24:52.134 --> 00:24:54.684
principal reasons so many survived.

00:24:55.974 --> 00:24:58.504
So, on one level, this is a

00:24:58.514 --> 00:25:00.994
story of heroism and bravery.

00:25:01.879 --> 00:25:04.434
Raoul Wallenberg chose to go somewhere

00:25:04.444 --> 00:25:06.854
very dangerous, did something very

00:25:06.874 --> 00:25:10.464
difficult, and as a direct result, a

00:25:10.464 --> 00:25:12.604
very large number of people who would

00:25:12.644 --> 00:25:15.064
otherwise have been killed were not.

00:25:15.964 --> 00:25:19.134
But heroism is not the whole story.

00:25:19.844 --> 00:25:22.294
The same family whose bank helped

00:25:22.304 --> 00:25:25.054
Germany finance the war, and whose

00:25:25.054 --> 00:25:27.274
company supplied ball bearings to

00:25:27.274 --> 00:25:30.508
the Nazi war machine into late 1944,

00:25:31.114 --> 00:25:32.814
also produced Raoul Wallenberg.

00:25:34.054 --> 00:25:36.474
And the same country that allowed

00:25:36.484 --> 00:25:38.524
hundreds of thousands of German soldiers

00:25:38.804 --> 00:25:41.594
across its railways, that sold iron

00:25:41.594 --> 00:25:43.504
ore to Germany throughout the war,

00:25:44.024 --> 00:25:46.754
also sent Wallenberg to Budapest.

00:25:48.214 --> 00:25:50.214
And this is not a story

00:25:50.424 --> 00:25:51.594
with a clean ending.

00:25:52.094 --> 00:25:55.204
The full KGB files have never been opened.

00:25:55.714 --> 00:25:58.404
What exactly happened in Lubyanka in

00:25:58.404 --> 00:26:02.704
1947 remains, officially, unconfirmed.

00:26:03.654 --> 00:26:05.914
But the legacy of Raoul

00:26:05.914 --> 00:26:07.664
Wallenberg is unmistakable.

00:26:08.414 --> 00:26:09.934
It's impossible to calculate the

00:26:09.934 --> 00:26:11.994
true number of people who owe their

00:26:12.004 --> 00:26:14.544
existence to what he did in Budapest

00:26:14.674 --> 00:26:17.364
— the thousands he saved, the children

00:26:17.364 --> 00:26:19.854
born to them, and the generations

00:26:19.864 --> 00:26:22.804
that followed — but it surely runs

00:26:22.954 --> 00:26:24.514
into the hundreds of thousands.

00:26:25.444 --> 00:26:26.914
It is certainly not without

00:26:26.914 --> 00:26:29.184
justification that he is remembered

00:26:29.464 --> 00:26:31.424
as the Angel of Budapest.

00:26:32.994 --> 00:26:35.344
OK, then, that is it for today's

00:26:35.374 --> 00:26:37.404
episode on Raoul Wallenberg.

00:26:37.774 --> 00:26:39.114
I hope it's been an interesting one

00:26:39.534 --> 00:26:41.114
and that you've learnt something new.

00:26:41.834 --> 00:26:43.644
You've been listening to English Learning

00:26:43.644 --> 00:26:46.304
for Curious Minds by Leonardo English.

00:26:46.794 --> 00:26:49.584
I'm Alastair Budge, you stay safe, and

00:26:49.584 --> 00:26:51.704
I'll catch you in the next episode.

